1
00:00:00,403 --> 00:00:05,812
October 19th, 1982 A hotel room near Los Angeles

2
00:00:05,832 --> 00:00:06,604
airport.

3
00:00:07,321 --> 00:00:10,593
A tall man in an expensive suit opens a suitcase,

4
00:00:10,619 --> 00:00:12,455
lifts a bag of white powder,

5
00:00:12,481 --> 00:00:14,928
and smiles at the camera hidden in the wall.

6
00:00:16,363 --> 00:00:17,747
It's better than gold,

7
00:00:17,773 --> 00:00:18,678
he says.

8
00:00:19,398 --> 00:00:20,529
Seconds later,

9
00:00:20,555 --> 00:00:23,069
FBI agents walk through the door.

10
00:00:24,499 --> 00:00:26,401
The man was John DeLorean.

11
00:00:27,122 --> 00:00:29,070
Months earlier he had been one of the most

12
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:31,418
famous car executives in America.

13
00:00:32,135 --> 00:00:34,216
And the car that carried his name was about

14
00:00:34,236 --> 00:00:35,766
to disappear forever.

15
00:00:37,195 --> 00:00:39,808
This is the story of how a dream car was built

16
00:00:39,828 --> 00:00:40,893
in a war zone,

17
00:00:41,025 --> 00:00:43,073
sold at double its promised price,

18
00:00:43,179 --> 00:00:45,946
and dragged its creator into an FBI sting.

19
00:00:46,666 --> 00:00:47,478
And why,

20
00:00:47,571 --> 00:00:48,821
forty years later,

21
00:00:48,927 --> 00:00:50,537
it is worth more than ever.

22
00:00:54,555 --> 00:00:56,165
To understand the DeLorean,

23
00:00:56,217 --> 00:00:57,960
you have to understand the man.

24
00:00:58,681 --> 00:01:01,341
John Zachary DeLorean grew up in Detroit,

25
00:01:01,393 --> 00:01:03,296
the son of a factory worker.

26
00:01:04,013 --> 00:01:06,227
He studied engineering and joined General

27
00:01:06,247 --> 00:01:08,216
Motors in the 1950s.

28
00:01:09,651 --> 00:01:10,769
At Pontiac,

29
00:01:10,835 --> 00:01:13,541
he helped push a crazy idea past the company's

30
00:01:13,561 --> 00:01:14,466
own rules:

31
00:01:14,585 --> 00:01:17,371
put a big V8 engine into a mid-size family

32
00:01:17,391 --> 00:01:18,029
car.

33
00:01:18,750 --> 00:01:22,168
In 1964 it became the Pontiac GTO,

34
00:01:22,274 --> 00:01:24,741
and many historians call it the car that kicked

35
00:01:24,761 --> 00:01:26,384
off the muscle car era.

36
00:01:27,819 --> 00:01:29,535
His rise was fast.

37
00:01:30,256 --> 00:01:32,982
He became the youngest head of a GM division,

38
00:01:33,022 --> 00:01:34,698
and later ran Chevrolet,

39
00:01:34,804 --> 00:01:37,052
the biggest car brand in America.

40
00:01:37,769 --> 00:01:39,179
He wore long hair,

41
00:01:39,232 --> 00:01:40,276
dated models,

42
00:01:40,296 --> 00:01:42,464
and partied with Hollywood stars.

43
00:01:43,181 --> 00:01:45,948
Detroit had never seen an executive like him.

44
00:01:47,379 --> 00:01:50,345
In 1973 at the very top,

45
00:01:50,384 --> 00:01:52,553
he walked away from General Motors.

46
00:01:53,273 --> 00:01:55,681
He said the company had become too slow,

47
00:01:55,747 --> 00:01:57,609
too safe and too boring.

48
00:01:58,327 --> 00:02:00,401
He wanted to build his own car.

49
00:02:01,119 --> 00:02:02,742
An ethical sports car,

50
00:02:02,808 --> 00:02:03,699
he called it.

51
00:02:04,417 --> 00:02:05,155
Safe,

52
00:02:05,175 --> 00:02:05,940
efficient,

53
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:07,356
and built to last.

54
00:02:11,387 --> 00:02:13,841
DeLorean founded the DeLorean Motor Company

55
00:02:13,861 --> 00:02:16,766
in 1975 and hired the best names he could

56
00:02:16,786 --> 00:02:17,505
find.

57
00:02:18,226 --> 00:02:20,892
The body was drawn by Giorgetto Giugiaro of

58
00:02:20,912 --> 00:02:21,896
Italdesign,

59
00:02:22,002 --> 00:02:24,362
the man behind some of the most famous cars

60
00:02:24,382 --> 00:02:25,394
of the century.

61
00:02:26,819 --> 00:02:29,413
The skin would be brushed stainless steel.

62
00:02:30,134 --> 00:02:31,477
No paint at all.

63
00:02:32,195 --> 00:02:33,498
It would never rust,

64
00:02:33,538 --> 00:02:35,180
and it would look like nothing else on the

65
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:35,865
road.

66
00:02:37,283 --> 00:02:39,172
And the doors would open upward,

67
00:02:39,198 --> 00:02:40,276
like wings.

68
00:02:40,996 --> 00:02:43,298
To hold up those heavy steel doors,

69
00:02:43,324 --> 00:02:45,511
the team used torsion bars developed with

70
00:02:45,531 --> 00:02:46,582
help from Grumman,

71
00:02:46,701 --> 00:02:48,836
the aerospace company that built hardware

72
00:02:48,856 --> 00:02:50,625
for the Apollo moon missions.

73
00:02:52,043 --> 00:02:53,879
Even the name was a promise.

74
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,369
DMC-12.

75
00:02:57,086 --> 00:02:59,441
The twelve stood for the target price:

76
00:02:59,480 --> 00:03:01,143
twelve thousand dollars.

77
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:04,486
A futuristic car for the price of an ordinary

78
00:03:04,506 --> 00:03:05,119
one.

79
00:03:06,563 --> 00:03:08,997
But the early prototypes had problems.

80
00:03:09,718 --> 00:03:12,397
So DeLorean turned to Colin Chapman and Lotus

81
00:03:12,417 --> 00:03:14,858
in England to re-engineer almost the entire

82
00:03:14,878 --> 00:03:15,530
car.

83
00:03:16,247 --> 00:03:17,092
It worked,

84
00:03:17,112 --> 00:03:18,362
but it was expensive,

85
00:03:18,415 --> 00:03:20,543
and the bill would come back to haunt him.

86
00:03:24,571 --> 00:03:26,686
Now DeLorean needed a factory,

87
00:03:26,725 --> 00:03:29,059
and he found the most unlikely place to build

88
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:29,558
one:

89
00:03:29,651 --> 00:03:30,476
Dunmurry,

90
00:03:30,515 --> 00:03:32,165
on the edge of Belfast,

91
00:03:32,191 --> 00:03:33,455
Northern Ireland.

92
00:03:34,891 --> 00:03:36,793
In the late 1970s,

93
00:03:36,859 --> 00:03:38,688
Northern Ireland was in the middle of the

94
00:03:38,708 --> 00:03:39,533
Troubles.

95
00:03:40,253 --> 00:03:41,132
Bombings,

96
00:03:41,171 --> 00:03:43,445
riots and soldiers on the streets.

97
00:03:44,163 --> 00:03:46,903
Unemployment in West Belfast was brutal.

98
00:03:48,331 --> 00:03:50,346
The British government made him an offer he

99
00:03:50,366 --> 00:03:51,603
couldn't refuse.

100
00:03:52,324 --> 00:03:53,667
Build your car here,

101
00:03:53,707 --> 00:03:55,423
and we will pay for most of it.

102
00:03:56,140 --> 00:03:58,487
Around one hundred million pounds of public

103
00:03:58,507 --> 00:04:00,343
money went into the project.

104
00:04:01,771 --> 00:04:02,682
In return,

105
00:04:02,702 --> 00:04:05,349
the factory promised thousands of jobs.

106
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:07,214
And for a while,

107
00:04:07,280 --> 00:04:08,198
it delivered.

108
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:11,169
Catholic and Protestant workers came in through

109
00:04:11,189 --> 00:04:12,280
separate gates,

110
00:04:12,346 --> 00:04:14,940
but worked side by side on the same line.

111
00:04:16,363 --> 00:04:18,079
In early 1981,

112
00:04:18,145 --> 00:04:20,539
the first cars rolled out of Dunmurry.

113
00:04:21,260 --> 00:04:22,710
The dream was real.

114
00:04:26,739 --> 00:04:28,455
Then the problems began.

115
00:04:29,176 --> 00:04:31,616
The car that was supposed to cost twelve thousand

116
00:04:31,636 --> 00:04:34,249
dollars arrived in showrooms at around twenty-five

117
00:04:34,269 --> 00:04:35,094
thousand.

118
00:04:35,812 --> 00:04:38,166
That was more than a Chevrolet Corvette.

119
00:04:39,603 --> 00:04:40,734
And for that money,

120
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,181
buyers got a car that was not fast.

121
00:04:43,902 --> 00:04:47,432
Its Peugeot-Renault-Volvo V6 made around 130

122
00:04:47,452 --> 00:04:49,381
horsepower in American trim.

123
00:04:50,098 --> 00:04:52,499
It needed about ten seconds to reach sixty

124
00:04:52,519 --> 00:04:53,756
miles per hour.

125
00:04:55,179 --> 00:04:57,859
Early owners reported doors that got stuck,

126
00:04:57,879 --> 00:04:59,249
electrics that failed,

127
00:04:59,315 --> 00:05:01,111
and panels that didn't line up.

128
00:05:01,831 --> 00:05:04,824
Stainless steel also showed every fingerprint.

129
00:05:06,243 --> 00:05:07,294
Worst of all,

130
00:05:07,334 --> 00:05:08,983
the timing was terrible.

131
00:05:09,704 --> 00:05:14,093
America fell into a recession in 1981 and 1982

132
00:05:14,824 --> 00:05:18,128
Interest rates were sky high Thousands of

133
00:05:18,148 --> 00:05:21,220
unsold DeLoreans sat waiting in parking lots

134
00:05:22,659 --> 00:05:24,482
The company was burning money.

135
00:05:25,202 --> 00:05:28,427
In February 1982 the British government put

136
00:05:28,447 --> 00:05:30,948
DeLorean Motor Cars into receivership.

137
00:05:31,665 --> 00:05:33,919
John DeLorean had months to find the money

138
00:05:33,939 --> 00:05:35,309
to save his company.

139
00:05:39,347 --> 00:05:40,697
Desperate for cash,

140
00:05:40,717 --> 00:05:43,210
DeLorean began talking to a man who claimed

141
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:45,279
he could arrange a huge investment.

142
00:05:45,999 --> 00:05:48,287
That man was a government informant.

143
00:05:49,715 --> 00:05:51,158
Over several meetings,

144
00:05:51,178 --> 00:05:54,343
the FBI secretly recorded the conversations.

145
00:05:55,064 --> 00:05:57,478
The plan on the table was a cocaine deal worth

146
00:05:57,498 --> 00:05:59,453
around twenty-four million dollars,

147
00:05:59,506 --> 00:06:01,387
with the profits meant to keep the company

148
00:06:01,407 --> 00:06:02,219
alive.

149
00:06:03,659 --> 00:06:07,895
On October 19th, 1982 in that hotel room near

150
00:06:07,915 --> 00:06:08,746
the airport,

151
00:06:08,766 --> 00:06:10,122
the trap closed.

152
00:06:10,843 --> 00:06:13,031
The arrest video was played on television

153
00:06:13,051 --> 00:06:14,182
around the world.

154
00:06:14,899 --> 00:06:16,043
The same week,

155
00:06:16,069 --> 00:06:18,623
the Dunmurry factory was shut for good.

156
00:06:20,051 --> 00:06:21,913
But the story has a twist.

157
00:06:22,634 --> 00:06:26,531
In 1984 a jury found DeLorean not guilty.

158
00:06:27,249 --> 00:06:29,290
His lawyers argued that the government had

159
00:06:29,310 --> 00:06:30,175
entrapped him,

160
00:06:30,267 --> 00:06:31,584
and the jury agreed.

161
00:06:33,011 --> 00:06:34,275
He walked free.

162
00:06:34,996 --> 00:06:36,313
But his reputation,

163
00:06:36,339 --> 00:06:38,733
his fortune and his company were gone.

164
00:06:39,451 --> 00:06:41,731
Investigations into where the company's money

165
00:06:41,751 --> 00:06:43,866
had gone would continue for years.

166
00:06:47,899 --> 00:06:48,751
In the end,

167
00:06:48,803 --> 00:06:51,650
only about nine thousand DeLoreans were built.

168
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:53,900
It should have been the end.

169
00:06:54,618 --> 00:06:56,866
A failed car from a failed company,

170
00:06:56,918 --> 00:06:58,648
forgotten in a few years.

171
00:07:00,067 --> 00:07:00,706
Then,

172
00:07:00,732 --> 00:07:04,190
in 1985 a movie changed everything.

173
00:07:04,911 --> 00:07:07,324
A Hollywood comedy about time travel chose

174
00:07:07,344 --> 00:07:09,771
a stainless steel car with gull-wing doors

175
00:07:09,791 --> 00:07:11,135
as its time machine.

176
00:07:11,852 --> 00:07:12,683
Overnight,

177
00:07:12,703 --> 00:07:15,011
the DeLorean became the most famous car in

178
00:07:15,031 --> 00:07:15,816
the world.

179
00:07:17,251 --> 00:07:17,936
Today,

180
00:07:17,956 --> 00:07:20,050
the cars that nobody wanted are collector

181
00:07:20,070 --> 00:07:20,922
pieces.

182
00:07:21,643 --> 00:07:24,229
Clean examples often sell for far more than

183
00:07:24,249 --> 00:07:25,673
their original price.

184
00:07:26,390 --> 00:07:28,976
A company in Texas bought the leftover parts

185
00:07:28,996 --> 00:07:30,606
and still keeps them running.

186
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:36,251
John DeLorean died in 2005 at 80 years old

187
00:07:36,972 --> 00:07:38,794
He never built another car.

188
00:07:39,512 --> 00:07:42,145
But the one he did build outlived his company,

189
00:07:42,198 --> 00:07:44,113
his scandal and his critics.

190
00:07:45,547 --> 00:07:47,582
So was the DeLorean a failure?

191
00:07:48,303 --> 00:07:49,407
As a business,

192
00:07:49,447 --> 00:07:50,564
absolutely.

193
00:07:51,282 --> 00:07:52,266
As a car,

194
00:07:52,332 --> 00:07:53,397
it was flawed.

195
00:07:54,114 --> 00:07:55,245
But as a dream,

196
00:07:55,324 --> 00:07:57,618
it might be one of the most successful cars

197
00:07:57,638 --> 00:07:58,490
ever made.

198
00:07:59,923 --> 00:08:02,025
If you want the next forgotten story,

199
00:08:02,117 --> 00:08:04,305
tell me in the comments which car or brand

200
00:08:04,325 --> 00:08:05,961
we should bring back to life.

201
00:08:06,682 --> 00:08:09,541
The most liked comment becomes the next episode.

202
00:08:10,259 --> 00:08:12,294
This is Salimofff Garage.
